Assess the breast using both views together. Consider density first,
then findings, then the overall BI-RADS category.

Definitions
- Density: A = almost entirely fatty; B = scattered areas of fibroglandular
  density; C = heterogeneously dense, may obscure small masses;
  D = extremely dense, lowers mammographic sensitivity.
- Findings (mark 1 only for suspicious findings that warrant follow-up;
  do not mark clearly benign findings; 1 if present in either view):
  mass, suspicious_calcification, asymmetry (including focal/global),
  architectural_distortion.
- BI-RADS: 1 = negative; 2 = benign finding(s); 3 = probably benign;
  4 = suspicious; 5 = highly suggestive of malignancy.

Consistency
- If any finding is 1, breast_birads must be 3, 4 or 5.
- If all findings are 0, breast_birads must be 1 or 2.
- Use the full range of options. In a screening population most breasts
  are BI-RADS 1; do not default to the middle category.

Return ONLY this JSON, with integer 0/1 values and no other text:
{"breast_density": "<A|B|C|D>",
 "findings": {"mass": <0|1>, "suspicious_calcification": <0|1>,
              "asymmetry": <0|1>, "architectural_distortion": <0|1>},
 "breast_birads": <1|2|3|4|5>}<|im_end|>
<|im_start|>assistant
{"breast_density": "C", "findings": {"mass": 0, "suspicious_calcification": 0, "asymmetry": 0, "architectural_distortion": 0}, "breast_birads": 2}<|im_end|>

